From 50862b1b24fb2feeca3ed79b5c5a734073aa36d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a monitor for the next start is confirmed on
 every path

The question whether to keep a monitor that only a start of Kodi takes
was armed only where the user said to restart now. Saying "not now", a
change on the same card that is left for the next start (from JSON-RPC,
or with the display asleep), and a move that left Kodi on no output also
leave the setting naming a display that nobody saw Kodi on: the next
start used it without a question, and a display that shows nothing had
nothing to undo it. Each of them is noted down now (ArmsFor(),
NoteFor()), against the value Kodi shows itself with; where the note
cannot be written, the setting keeps its value and the user is told.

What a start does is decided and noted down before it chooses its
output (AtBegin()): the stage after this one is written first, with this
start's value among the refused, so that a start that ends before its
interface (a driver that fails on the other card) does not take the same
display again. A start that cannot write that does not use its value
but the next one (Unwritten()). Kodi is started again only once what the
next start uses is written, and never while something plays: it waits
for playback to end, and a stop in between leaves it to the next start.
The 90 seconds for the question count from when the interface is up.

Where neither the monitor chosen nor the one of before is kept, the
setting falls to Default, and that start leaves out every display that
was not kept in the sequence where another one can be used
(WithoutRefused(), in the choice of CDRMUtils::OpenDrm() and
FindConnector()); the log and a notification say what happened. Where
what the next start uses cannot be written after a "no", Kodi stays
where it is and says so.

The texts name the displays as the setting lists them (ValueLabel()),
with the graphics card where two cards have displays, not by the value
of the setting.

Tested on the host with a simulation of the starts that uses the real
choice of the output, and with mutations of each rule.
